## The problem

Analysing a dataset usually means writing Pandas by hand. This platform lets people upload structured data and ask questions in plain English, then get back tables and charts they can trust.

## How it works

- **Multi-stage agent workflow.** LangGraph coordinates query interpretation, dataset inspection, analysis planning, code generation, execution and response validation as reusable stages.
- **Sandboxed execution.** Generated code runs in an isolated Python sandbox that supports Pandas transformations and Plotly visualisations without touching the core application.
- **Typed APIs.** A FastAPI backend exposes typed endpoints to the Next.js frontend, with JWT access and refresh token flows.

## Engineering

Frontend, backend, database and execution sandbox are separate Docker services, which keeps responsibilities clear and deployment predictable.
